ent-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8333214</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9175919-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9175919</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1120039A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KASE RIEKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAWAI HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KASE, RIEKO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWAI, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KASE RIEKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAWAI HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KASE, RIEKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWAI, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Compositions for preventing plant disease injury which promote the formation of phytoalexin (i.e., an antibacterial substance sustained by plants per se) so as to enhance the resistance to disease injury inherent to the plants, little damage the environment and are inexpensive and highly safe. These compositions contain a mixture of at least one sulfur-containing amino acid selected from methionine, cysteine and cystine with D-glucose. These compositions are sprayed, either as such or after diluting 1 to 100,000-fold with water, onto the above-ground parts of plants. Alternatively, they are mixed directly with soil or soil is drenched with the compositions diluted 1 to 1,000,000-fold with water.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne des compositions permettant de prévenir les maladies de plantes. Ces compositions activent la formation de phytoalexine (une substance antibactérienne produit par les plantes elles-mêmes) permettant ainsi d'améliorer la résistance aux maladies inhérente aux plantes avec une charge minimale pour l'environnement, un faible coût et une sécurité élevée. Ces compositions contiennent un mélange comprenant au moins un acide aminé sulfureux, sélectionné dans le groupe composé par la méthionine, la cystéine et la cystine avec D-glucose. Ces compositions sont vaporisées, soit telles quelles soit après une dilution de 1/1 à 1/100 000 dans l'eau, sur les parties aériennes de plantes. Dans un autre mode d'application elles sont mélangées directement au sol, ou le sol est imbibé de ces compositions diluées à raison de 1/1 à 1/1 000 000 dans de l'eau.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>